* ============================================================
* SSVEP 5-KEY WHEELCHAIR STIMULUS PANEL - CIRCUIT NETLIST
* Project: Extraction of Robust Commands from SSVEP Signals
* Author reference for: Farooq - University of Tabriz
* Supervisor: Prof. Hadi Seyedarabi
*
* FORMAT: This is a human-readable "as-built" netlist, not a
* CAD-tool-generated file. It lists every component (with a
* reference designator) and every net (a net = a wire that
* connects two or more pins together at the same electrical
* point).
*
* IMPORTANT - VERIFY BEFORE BUILDING:
* Pin numbers for ULN2003AG and STM32F103C8T6 below are written
* from standard datasheet pinouts. Confirm every pin number
* against YOUR component's actual datasheet before soldering.
* A wrong pin number here could damage a component.
* ============================================================


* ---------------------------------------------------------
* SECTION 1: COMPONENT LIST (Reference Designators)
* ---------------------------------------------------------

BT1     : Li-ion battery cell (single cell, ~3.7V nominal)          [not in your parts list - confirm you have one]
U1      : TP4056                  - battery charge controller
U2      : XL6009E1                - DC-DC boost converter
U3      : L7805CV (#1)            - linear regulator, LOGIC 5V rail
U4      : L7805CV (#2)            - linear regulator, LED 5V rail
U5      : STM32F103C8T6 Blue Pill - main microcontroller (MCU)
U6      : ULN2003AG               - Darlington driver array (7 channels, 5 used)
U7      : HC-05                   - Bluetooth serial module
RLDR1   : Photoresistor (LDR)     - light sensor for verification
R18     : Fixed resistor, ~10k ohm - photoresistor divider (VERIFY value against your LDR's datasheet)
C1, C2  : ~0.33uF / ~0.1uF        - U3 input/output caps (typical L7805 app values - VERIFY datasheet)
C3, C4  : ~0.33uF / ~0.1uF        - U4 input/output caps (typical L7805 app values - VERIFY datasheet)
SW1     : Power switch (optional) - master on/off

D1, D2, D3       : Forward key LEDs   (3x)
D4, D5, D6       : Backward key LEDs  (3x)
D7, D8, D9       : Left key LEDs      (3x)
D10, D11, D12    : Right key LEDs     (3x)
D13-D17          : STOP key LEDs      (5x)

R1-R3   : ~105 ohm - series resistor per Forward LED  (D1,D2,D3)
R4-R6   : ~105 ohm - series resistor per Backward LED (D4,D5,D6)
R7-R9   : ~105 ohm - series resistor per Left LED     (D7,D8,D9)
R10-R12 : ~105 ohm - series resistor per Right LED    (D10,D11,D12)
R13-R17 : ~105 ohm - series resistor per STOP LED     (D13-D17)


* ---------------------------------------------------------
* SECTION 2: NET LIST (Net_Name : connected pins)
* ---------------------------------------------------------

NET_BATT+     : BT1.+, U1.B+
NET_BATT-     : BT1.-, U1.B-, GND
GND           : U1.GND, U2.GND, U3.GND(pin2), U4.GND(pin2), U5.GND,
                U6.GND(pin8/E), U7.GND, RLDR1.bottom(via R18), SW1.common,
                C1.-, C2.-, C3.-, C4.-

NET_CHG_OUT   : U1.OUT+, U2.VIN      (TP4056 charged output feeds boost converter input)

NET_BOOST_OUT : U2.VOUT, U3.VIN(pin1), U4.VIN(pin1), C1.+, C3.+
                (Set U2 output ~9V using its onboard trimpot/feedback resistors
                 - VERIFY actual output with multimeter BEFORE connecting U3/U4)

NET_5V_LOGIC  : U3.VOUT(pin3), U5.5V_pin, U7.VCC, C2.+
                (This rail powers the Blue Pill's onboard 3.3V regulator
                 and the HC-05 module - kept separate from LED rail on purpose)

NET_5V_LED    : U4.VOUT(pin3), U6.COM(pin9), C4.+,
                R1.pin1, R2.pin1, R3.pin1,      (Forward LEDs anode side)
                R4.pin1, R5.pin1, R6.pin1,      (Backward LEDs anode side)
                R7.pin1, R8.pin1, R9.pin1,      (Left LEDs anode side)
                R10.pin1, R11.pin1, R12.pin1,   (Right LEDs anode side)
                R13.pin1, R14.pin1, R15.pin1, R16.pin1, R17.pin1  (STOP LEDs anode side)

* ---- Forward key (12 Hz) ----
NET_GPIO_PA0    : U5.PA0, U6.IN1(pin1)
NET_ULN_OUT1    : U6.OUT1(pin16), D1.cathode, D2.cathode, D3.cathode
NET_R1_D1       : R1.pin2, D1.anode
NET_R2_D2       : R2.pin2, D2.anode
NET_R3_D3       : R3.pin2, D3.anode

* ---- Backward key (8 Hz) ----
NET_GPIO_PA1    : U5.PA1, U6.IN2(pin2)
NET_ULN_OUT2    : U6.OUT2(pin15), D4.cathode, D5.cathode, D6.cathode
NET_R4_D4       : R4.pin2, D4.anode
NET_R5_D5       : R5.pin2, D5.anode
NET_R6_D6       : R6.pin2, D6.anode

* ---- Left key (13 Hz) ----
NET_GPIO_PA2    : U5.PA2, U6.IN3(pin3)
NET_ULN_OUT3    : U6.OUT3(pin14), D7.cathode, D8.cathode, D9.cathode
NET_R7_D7       : R7.pin2, D7.anode
NET_R8_D8       : R8.pin2, D8.anode
NET_R9_D9       : R9.pin2, D9.anode

* ---- Right key (9 Hz) ----
NET_GPIO_PA3    : U5.PA3, U6.IN4(pin4)
NET_ULN_OUT4    : U6.OUT4(pin13), D10.cathode, D11.cathode, D12.cathode
NET_R10_D10     : R10.pin2, D10.anode
NET_R11_D11     : R11.pin2, D11.anode
NET_R12_D12     : R12.pin2, D12.anode

* ---- STOP key (10 Hz) - safety critical, isolated on TIM3 ----
NET_GPIO_PA6    : U5.PA6, U6.IN5(pin5)
NET_ULN_OUT5    : U6.OUT5(pin12), D13.cathode, D14.cathode, D15.cathode, D16.cathode, D17.cathode
NET_R13_D13     : R13.pin2, D13.anode
NET_R14_D14     : R14.pin2, D14.anode
NET_R15_D15     : R15.pin2, D15.anode
NET_R16_D16     : R16.pin2, D16.anode
NET_R17_D17     : R17.pin2, D17.anode

* ---- Photoresistor verification divider ----
NET_3V3         : U5.3V3_pin, RLDR1.top
NET_LDR_MID     : RLDR1.bottom, R18.pin1, U5.PA4(ADC12_IN4), [scope probe point]
NET_LDR_GND     : R18.pin2, GND

* ---- HC-05 Bluetooth sync link ----
NET_UART_TX     : U5.PA9(USART1_TX), U7.RXD
NET_UART_RX     : U5.PA10(USART1_RX), U7.TXD

* ---------------------------------------------------------
* END OF NETLIST
* Unused ULN2003AG channels: IN6/OUT6, IN7/OUT7 - leave
* unconnected (spare capacity for a future 6th/7th command key).
* ---------------------------------------------------------
